== (1) CM scan, W(R)=exp(-c R^alpha), c=1, n<=8 ==
   R window [0.1, min(100,17^(1/alpha))]: below 0.1 the Cauchy formula for n=8 loses all digits,
   above it W<1e-8 and f^(n) is not resolvable in double precision
  alpha   R-range          sign-fails (-1)^n W^(n)<0       realness   verdict
   0.1   [1.0e-01,1.0e+02]  -                                     4.4e-11   IN (CM)
   0.3   [1.0e-01,1.0e+02]  -                                     1.3e-11   IN (CM)
   0.5   [1.0e-01,1.0e+02]  -                                     8.6e-12   IN (CM)
   0.7   [1.0e-01,5.7e+01]  -                                     5.6e-12   IN (CM)
   0.9   [1.0e-01,2.3e+01]  -                                     2.7e-11   IN (CM)
   1.0   [1.0e-01,1.7e+01]  -                                     1.8e-09   IN (CM)
   1.2   [1.0e-01,1.1e+01]  n=2@R=0.1 n=2@R=0.126261              1.9e-11   OUT
   1.5   [1.0e-01,6.6e+00]  n=2@R=0.1 n=2@R=0.123315              6.6e-11   OUT
   2.0   [1.0e-01,4.1e+00]  n=2@R=0.1 n=2@R=0.120437              2.0e-11   OUT
   3.0   [1.0e-01,2.6e+00]  n=2@R=0.1 n=2@R=0.117627              1.1e-13   OUT

== (2) witness alpha=1/2: Levy(1/2) density, exact identity ==
   density closed form = t^-3/2 exp(-1/4t)/(2 sqrt pi): min on t in [1e-2,1e2] = 3.922e-09 > 0
   Int dens dt = 0.999930373474
   max rel err  |Int e^-tR p(t)dt - e^-sqrt R|  over R in {.1,.5,1,4,25} = 2.1e-16
   => e^-sqrt(R) IS a Bernstein profile of a POSITIVE measure: 0<W<=1, no power law

== (3) engine: x^alpha = (alpha/Gamma(1-alpha)) Int_0^inf (1-e^-xt) t^-1-alpha dt ==
   alpha=0.3: formula=1.1725541909  x^alpha=1.1725589243  relerr=4.0e-06   (kernel (1-e^-xt)t^-1-a >= 0 => Bernstein function for alpha in (0,1))
   alpha=0.5: formula=1.3038404752  x^alpha=1.3038404810  relerr=4.5e-09   (kernel (1-e^-xt)t^-1-a >= 0 => Bernstein function for alpha in (0,1))
   alpha=0.7: formula=1.4498067767  x^alpha=1.4498205291  relerr=9.5e-06   (kernel (1-e^-xt)t^-1-a >= 0 => Bernstein function for alpha in (0,1))

== (4) alpha>1: W'' = c a R^(a-2) e^-cR^a (c a R^a - (a-1)), c=1 ==
   alpha=1.2: W''<0 on (0,R*), R*=((a-1)/a)^(1/a)=0.224668; min W''=-6.018e+01 => NOT CM
   alpha=1.5: W''<0 on (0,R*), R*=((a-1)/a)^(1/a)=0.480750; min W''=-2.371e+01 => NOT CM
   alpha=2.0: W''<0 on (0,R*), R*=((a-1)/a)^(1/a)=0.707107; min W''=-2.000e+00 => NOT CM
   alpha=3.0: W''<0 on (0,R*), R*=((a-1)/a)^(1/a)=0.873580; min W''=-2.151e+00 => NOT CM

== (5) log-power, EXACT profile: W = exp(-c (Log z)^beta) ==
   (a) branch: (Log z)^beta is non-real across R in (0,1) for beta not an integer
   beta= 0.3: Im W(R+i0)=-3.916e-01  Im W(R-i0)=+3.916e-01  Re-jump=0.000e+00  -> real-valued CM W cannot match
   beta= 0.5: Im W(R+i0)=-7.397e-01  Im W(R-i0)=+7.397e-01  Re-jump=0.000e+00  -> real-valued CM W cannot match
   beta= 0.7: Im W(R+i0)=-9.232e-01  Im W(R-i0)=+9.232e-01  Re-jump=0.000e+00  -> real-valued CM W cannot match
   beta= 1.5: Im W(R+i0)=+5.456e-01  Im W(R-i0)=-5.456e-01  Re-jump=0.000e+00  -> real-valued CM W cannot match
   beta= 2.5: Im W(R+i0)=-3.894e-01  Im W(R-i0)=+3.894e-01  Re-jump=0.000e+00  -> real-valued CM W cannot match
   (b) integer beta: endpoint limit vs W(0+) = mu(R_+) in [0,1]
       (entries under e^-709 are clipped; the point is the limit, not the value)
   beta=1: W(1e-6)=1.000e+06  W(1e6)=1.000e-06   -> unbounded as R->0 => |W|>1
   beta=2: W(1e-6)=1.279e-83  W(1e6)=1.279e-83   -> W->0 as R->0 => mu=0 => W=0 (contradiction)
   beta=3: W(1e-6)=8.218e+307  W(1e6)=1.217e-308   -> unbounded as R->0 => |W|>1
   beta=4: W(1e-6)=1.217e-308  W(1e6)=1.217e-308   -> W->0 as R->0 => mu=0 => W=0 (contradiction)

== (6) log-power, ASYMPTOTIC profile: rho(t)=t^-1 exp(-c|ln t|^beta), c=1 ==
   parametrise R=e^L; g(u)=-e^(L+u)-|u|^beta, ln W = max g + log Int exp(g-max g) du
   beta=0.5: -lnW/L^beta at L=10,30,100,300,600: 0.3605 0.5554 0.7146 0.8180 0.8656   -> c=1; local exponent beta_eff(L=100..600) = 0.607
   beta=1.0: -lnW/L^beta at L=10,30,100,300,600: 1.0000 1.0000 1.0000 1.0000 1.0000   -> c=1; local exponent beta_eff(L=100..600) = 1.000
   beta=2.0: -lnW/L^beta at L=10,30,100,300,600: 0.6865 0.8129 0.9170 0.9645 0.9798   -> c=1; local exponent beta_eff(L=100..600) = 2.037
   beta=3.0: -lnW/L^beta at L=10,30,100,300,600: 0.2579 0.4881 0.7509 0.8900 0.9371   -> c=1; local exponent beta_eff(L=100..600) = 3.124

== (7) R^-p (ln R)^q ==
   q>0: d/dR[R^-p L^q] = R^-p-1 L^q-1 (q - p L) changes sign at ln R=q/p
     p=2.0,q=1.0: sign change at ln R=0.500 => not monotone => NOT CM
     p=2.0,q=2.0: sign change at ln R=1.000 => not monotone => NOT CM
   q<0 (necessary-condition scan n<=8; R>=2 keeps the branch point R=1 outside the circle):
     p=0.0 q=-1.0: sign-fails=-                    realness=1.9e-05
     p=0.5 q=-1.0: sign-fails=-                    realness=2.2e-06
     p=1.0 q=-2.0: sign-fails=-                    realness=3.4e-07
     p=2.0 q=-0.5: sign-fails=-                    realness=8.2e-08

== (8) allowed set: gapped and gapless members both present ==
   member                   W(0+)   max W   p_eff=-dlnW/dlnR@[10,100]   class
   delta_m (m=0.7)         1.0000  1.0000                27.3606   gapped  W<=e^-0.7R
   U[1,2] uniform          1.0000  1.0000                40.0865   gapped  W<=e^-R
   stable alpha=0.5        0.9999  0.9999                 2.9696   no gap  exp(-sqrt R)
   stable alpha=0.3        0.9960  0.9960                 0.8624   no gap  exp(-R^0.3)
   stable alpha=0.9        1.0000  1.0000                23.9524   no gap  stretched exp
   => both a gapped and a gapless member: the two constraints have zero polarity on the gap

== (9) gap criterion: rate = inf supp rho ==
   rho=U[0.3,1.0]:  R*W(R)/e^-0.3R  = 0.5034 0.9991 1.0000 1.0000   -> 1: rate = a = inf supp rho
   rho=U[0.7,2.0]:  R*W(R)/e^-0.7R  = 0.7275 1.0000 1.0000 1.0000   -> 1: rate = a = inf supp rho
   rho=U[1e-4,1]: R*W(R) at R=1e4 = 3.679e-01 vs e^-1 = 3.679e-01  -> rate 1e-4: mass near 0 sets the rate
